      <h2>A maths topic each, explained to the parents</h2>
      <p>Each Lower Secondary student was given a different maths topic from the quarter, such as square and cube numbers, and made a poster to explain it. At the showcase they talked their parents through their topic and the reasoning behind it, then turned the questions on them with a short quiz, worked out on sticky notes and small whiteboards.</p>
      <p>They also showed the models they made in Art of Science, the art class that goes with their Cambridge Science, and the class reading wall, which keeps count of the books they read through the year.</p>
